&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AMER Product Demand Generation is a team of marketers that drive strategies to engage prospects and customers, generating demand for Stripe&#39;s priority products in the Americas. We partner closely with Campaigns, Product Marketing, Sales Development, and Sales to bring full-funnel campaigns to life and optimize performance and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced marketer to lead Money Management marketing across the US, Canada, and Latin America. Money Management brings together products that help businesses hold funds, move money globally, create and manage cards, and access financing. You’ll set the regional strategy and turn it into programs that build demand, grow pipeline, and help increase market share in partnership with teams across Stripe’s go-to-market organization. You’ll also help Stripe strengthen its approach to marketing Money Management and evolve demand generation for this high-priority area for Stripe. Money Management is still in an early stage of its marketing journey, with a strong opportunity to shape the strategy, build the programs that bring it to market, and establish how we create demand across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will have a meaningful impact across Stripe’s go-to-market organization. Money Management is a rapidly growing, high-priority product and an important part of Stripe’s strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll build and improve the engine that reaches key decision-makers and create a consistent experience across customer journeys, channels, and campaigns. You’ll set regional priorities, allocate budget across channels, and connect global campaign strategy with regional execution for Money Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional multi-channel strategy for Money Management marketing campaigns that drive demand. Channels can include paid media, content syndication, digital events, account based marketing (ABM), etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build region-specific marketing activations with channel leads to unlock local opportunities for Money Management audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a cross-GTM coalition including Global Campaigns, Events, Product Sales, Sales Development, and Sales Operations to jointly grow the Money Management pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics for Money Management across the sales funnel — investigating conversion, channel mix effectiveness, and pipeline health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to define regional requirements as Stripe refines marketing capabilities, MarTech stack, and lead management for scaled motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify innovative new ways to reach and engage the Money Management audience — there is broad leeway in this role to pursue creative marketing ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a thought leader representing the Americas as Stripe grows its Money Management go-to-market across campaigns and broader strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience running scaled digital demand generation programs (e.g., demand generation, growth marketing, or regional marketing)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GTM direct ownership of an audience or product segment at a B2B company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building multi-channel demand generation strategies and owning integrated digital activations across paid media, content marketing, email marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience assessing business health and managing marketing performance metrics. You can turn go-to-market data on lead generation, funnel conversion, pipeline progress, and channel performance into clear insights and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple complex programs simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building and delivering programs with partners across Sales, Sales Development, Product Marketing, Content, and Event Marketing. Be prepared to discuss programs you owned directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity: The ability to build, adapt, and maintain positive momentum is key for this role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI including leveraging native AI tooling and integrating LLM / agentic capabilities into everyday work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling net new programs with an eye toward repeatability and efficiency. You’ve built 0 to 1 and have scaled from 1 to 10&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event or field marketing experience or exposure (prior event ownership not required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or or adjacent industries or marketing FinTech solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adjacent business experience (e.g., strategy consulting, paid media, etc) that brings well-rounded GTM perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Brand Studio is a multi-disciplinary team that accelerates the awareness and trajectory of our brand. We craft the creative vision and strategy for different types of projects and audiences, and amplify them across various mediums, channels, objects to environments, and digital and physical experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe brand identity team is responsible for defining and evolving Stripe’s visual identity, and bringing the Stripe brand to life in new and impactful ways across surfaces. Our goal is to enable the creation of a coherent, high quality brand experience across the user journey, building recognition and trust in Stripe at every turn. We collaborate with other design systems teams to translate our brand for Stripe.com and Dashboard, and partner with teams across the company on high impact user-facing projects to create work that feels authentic to Stripe at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Motion Designers at Stripe demonstrate a passion for the craft of movement and a deep understanding of how motion communicates brand character. As a member of the Identity team, you will be responsible for defining and elevating Stripe&#39;s motion language across new and existing surfaces. Motion designers at Stripe demonstrate passion for great design and for expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible motion systems that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency for the brand at scale. The ideal candidate is technically fluent, crisply articulates motion decisions, and collaborates seamlessly with other designers, engineers, marketers, and agency partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute motion design direction across Stripe&#39;s brand ecosystem—from concept through final delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion and influence how the Stripe brand expresses itself through image and motion and develop guidelines, systems, and processes to ensure quality and consistency at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain Stripe&#39;s motion design system: principles, timing tokens, animation guidelines, and reusable motion components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with non-motion designers, elevating and informing each other’s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external motion and production studios or contractors in creative strategy, execution, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share motion knowledge and best practices with teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay curious and experimental as an avid maker, obsessed with tinkering and iterating to create beautiful things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape a strategic vision that pushes brand boundaries and builds internal awareness of design’s impact at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5+ years of relevant motion design experience for technical, brand-driven, or product-led organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert command of motion design tools: After Effects, Cinema 4D (or Houdini), AI tools, and the Adobe Creative Cloud suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong portfolio demonstrating high-craft motion work—including brand identity systems, campaign work, in-product animation, and/or data-driven motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of animation principles: timing, easing, staging, anticipation, and how motion communicates meaning and brand character&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a systems-thinker and excel at extrapolating and extending shared patterns and behaviors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of emerging motion and AI tools and how they fit into a professional production workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record delivering high-quality motion work independently, and in close collaboration with cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find a meaningful balance between optimizing for speed, quality, and doing challenging, interesting, frame-perfect work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions and crave feedback to help you design at your best&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and have them help you learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, with a drive for perfection down to the last frame&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about Stripe&#39;s mission, are dedicated to a user-first mindset, and have experience working with data and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

