&lt;li&gt;Own quota planning for the global Sales organization, including building and maintaining quota models, adapting them to organizational changes, and driving stakeholder alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze sales and go-to-market data to identify trends and channel efficiency, and develop models that inform planning, quota setting, and strategic decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and other go-to-market leaders to shape strategic priorities, translate future-state goals into actionable plans, and execute key initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and define KPIs that translate complex data into actionable insights for business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support high-priority cross-functional initiatives that improve execution and accelerate revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 2–4 years of experience in go-to-market, growth, or revenue strategy; management consulting; investment banking or equity research; business analysis; or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can break down complex or ambiguous business problems, identify key tradeoffs, and develop clear, actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong quantitative modeling and analytical skills, with attention to detail and the ability to communicate key insights to senior business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly in writing and verbally, including synthesizing complex concepts and developing presentations for senior and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
