&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a motivated Channel Partner professional to help grow and manage our partner ecosystem by identifying, onboarding, and enabling partners for long-term success. This role will focus on building strong relationships with resellers, managed service providers (MSPs), and regional partners to drive customer adoption and revenue growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity to join a fast-growing cloud software company, gain exposure to a high-impact ecosystem role, and contribute directly to Datadog’s growth across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Datadog, we value our office culture — the relationships and collaboration it builds, and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recruit, and onboard new channel partners to support regional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable and support existing partners through training, account alignment, and co-selling activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong day-to-day relationships with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Datadog sales teams to identify and drive partner-influenced opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate partner activities including enablement sessions, pipeline reviews, and joint account planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing and demand generation activities with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track partner performance, pipeline contribution, and engagement metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive partner-sourced pipeline and revenue growth across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in channel sales, partner management, or business development within a technology or SaaS company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with resellers, MSPs, or regional channel partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with sales and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and capable of managing multiple partner relationships simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable learning technical concepts and positioning value to partners and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with systems management or monitoring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with partnerships supporting DevOps, particularly in a cloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background/education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset with a passion for taking initiatives from ideation to impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for fast-paced, sometimes unpredictable growth culture and environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in identifying market opportunities with a track record of initiating go-to-market plans and sales follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
