&lt;p&gt;Datadog is seeking a Senior People Business Partner (PBP) to work closely with business&amp;nbsp; leadership and our People team to help support our growing cross-functional team in our Tokyo office. This position will work closely to support the needs of our go-to-market (GTM) team members in Japan while working strategically on all People programs and initiatives. Datadog has had exponential growth year-over-year and has no plans to stop - so there is a lot to learn from and contribute to our rapidly scaling team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as regional PBP for all employees in Japan across a variety of pre-sales, post-sales and related GTM support teams; represent our global PBP team to partner on the front line with all employees and leadership in Datadog’s Tokyo office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise, coach, and influence management on all things people-related, including: performance management, coaching, career pathing, employee relations, compensation, organizational development &amp;amp; scaling, training, culture, inclusion, employee engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain close partnership with departmental PBPs to collaborate on critical needs and change management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with the appropriate People Center of Excellence (COE) team to gather their expertise to provide input on program design to enhance the employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, advise and consult on People policies, guidelines, and programs with employee base, in collaboration with COE colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide analysis and consulting to leadership to drive data-driven people decisions and implementation of best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess employee development needs, make recommendations, and implement appropriate solutions aligned with the organization’s broader strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle complex global employee relations issues, working with leadership to implement best practices and approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in 5+ years as an HRBP or in a related HR role, preferably with experience in fast-growing technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to adapt your approach and pivot your skillset from strategic, high level program implementation to granular day-to-day needs of a fast paced business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in your analytical &amp;amp; reporting skills; solid experience with HRIS (Workday is a bonus!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in working across business functions with first line and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A master in your project management and organizational skills, with a proven ability to design clear processes, and a detail-oriented yet flexible approach to problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in employee relations and knowledge of global employment practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct, approachable, and friendly communication style and strong customer service orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills and able to build relationships and trust at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
