&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; AI coding agents now write code 100x faster than humans can review it, but new bottlenecks mean companies aren&#39;t shipping as fast as their agents can write code. We believe the major bottleneck is correctness, and it’s shifting from human code review to continuous, production-grounded validation at every stage of software delivery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://youtube.com/watch?si=xBkMradpv0Kj9yV-&amp;amp;t=3421&amp;amp;v=x7XuP8UCwzI&amp;amp;feature=youtu.be&quot;&gt;Bits Release&lt;/a&gt; is an early-stage product that carries every change through the release lifecycle: it reviews the code, validates the change before merge, follows the rollout through staging and production, detects regressions, simulates and proposes fixes, and converts what it catches into permanent safeguards. It fuses Datadog&#39;s production signals coupled with newer capabilities like &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/bits-testing-test-coverage/&quot;&gt;Bits Testing&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.datadoghq.com/tracing/live_debugger/&quot;&gt;Live Debugger&lt;/a&gt; in a single agentic harness, so companies can ship at the speed their agents write.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, narrative, and roadmap for Bits Release end to end, from pre-merge to continuous production validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customers, internal software engineers and design on a developer experience that earns developers&#39; trust and gets out of the way once it&#39;s earned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive packaging and pricing to a decision (per-investigation consumption vs. continuous platform capability) with finance and product leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat agent quality as the product. Own the evals, reliability targets, and KPIs that prove Bits Release works, and keep proving it as it scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior engineers who expect you to track the AI frontier, hold technical opinions, and stay close to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product marketing, advocacy, and sales to take Bits Release from preview to GA, with a story that lands for the SREs who buy it and the developers who use it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product management (or 4+ with a deep technical background), with meaningful time on developer tools, CI/CD, observability, or SRE/platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve shipped an LLM or agentic product: you know what good evals look like, how to debug nondeterministic systems, and how to weigh cost, latency, and quality tradeoffs in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI coding agents daily and have strong opinions about what releasing software means two to three years from now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep SDLC fluency: PR workflows, CI systems, deployment strategies (canary, blue-green, feature flags, progressive rollout), and production signals (traces, logs, RUM, synthetics, error tracking).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re at your best when the problem is still ambiguous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an exceptional writer and speaker. We write, sharpen, and defend our narratives continuously, often to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
